;  304
;  305    ! RUN_FILE runs the lines of the file NAME, named at COLUMN, as if each
;  306    ! were typed: for LOAD, the variables and functions are cleared first, and
;  307    ! every line is quiet. A line ending in an error ends the file, and every
;  308    ! file that ran it (ABANDON), each saying the line it was at: in the
;  309    ! innermost, the error is reported with the line itself, which the
;  310    ! terminal hasn't shown. QUIT or EXIT ends the file alone. Under SET ECHO
;  311    ! each line is shown after the prompt, as a typed line is (but not while
;  312    ! LOAD runs).
